//! The contract engine — generated from ONE declarative member list.
//!
//! `contract_universe!` (proc-macro, crate `mli-contract-macros`) expands the
//! `members` list into, in lockstep:
//! - [`ContractFactory`] — the box-free build+run enum (whole-universe);
//! - [`CatalogMeta`] + the `id -> contract` projections (`family_of` …
//!   `needs_volume_of`) — the metadata the optimizer prices config trees with;
//! - one narrow box-free **slot enum** per flagged id-subset (e.g. `SmootherSlot`
//!   from `+smoother`) — exactly the flagged members, the inline non-recursive
//!   container a composite holds for a configurable inner smoother.
//!
//! Adding an indicator = its `impl Indicator` + ONE `members` line here. The
//! factory and the catalog cannot drift — they ARE this list. A flagged member
//! subset becomes a narrow iterable slot enum by ONE `+flag` (e.g. `+smoother`).
//!
//! `flavor` selects the `MarketSample` arm; `family` is a TOKEN (the macro cannot
//! read the `FAMILY` const) — a generated test asserts token == `FAMILY[0]`.
//!
//! `contract_factory` / `contract_catalog` re-export from here for path stability;
//! the hand-written derived logic (weights, `family_members`) lives in
//! `contract_catalog` over these generated projections.

// LiquidationRate / OiZScore expose `value`/`is_ready`/`reset` through their
// consumer trait (not inherently) — the generated runtime calls them by method
// syntax, so the traits must be in scope. (BookImb's are inherent; all `update_*`
// are reached by fully-qualified UFCS inside the macro.)
